I specialize in analyzing various types of biological data, including RNAseq, single nucleotides, structural variants, copy number variants, and clinically relevant variables. My main focus is to discover biomarkers and drug targets for different diseases. I have experience in analyzing oncological datasets for lung cancer, multiple myeloma, prostate cancer, pancreatic cancer, and kidney cancer. I have worked with different data sources such as TCGA/GDC, Flatiron, ICGC, Tempus MMRF, and others. I am involved in all stages of the analysis process, from data preprocessing to model construction and interpretation. While my main tools are our proprietary causal Bayesian network learning and predictive tools, I also explore open source machine learning techniques that may be applicable to our datasets. For example, I have investigated unsupervised machine learning methods for tumor subclonal composition analysis and patient drug response stratification.

